       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Questions:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Can we track a list of the objects that have been reindexed?",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Do the objects come out of ocfl-java in a consistent order?",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Each object is reindexed in it’s own database transaction which is then committed, so we probably use the database as the record of already indexed children. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Direct/Indirect container relationships are generated ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "em"
           }
          ],
          "text": "after",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " all the other objects are indexed.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "So with some (Jared’s suggestion here) new flag to resume indexing, the server would re-run the IndexBuilder but skip any object with an entry in the ocflIndex or containmentIndex.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Alternative suggestion is to write a file on reindex of all processed objects. On Fedora startup if that file exists then continue reindexing. Once reindexing is complete, remove the file.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
